    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Brice Turang** (73.37) and **Corbin Carroll** (72.42) serving as our undisputed anchors. **Brice Turang** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and favorable delivery speed from Freeland, which heavily inflates his stolen base probability\u2014our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** continues to capitalize on a prime lineup position and a favorable right-handed matchup against Cavalli. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Josh Naylor** also project as \"Strong\" plays, with **Tyler Soderstrom** hitting in the heart of the order and **Josh Naylor** leveraging a +11% cumulative lift from park and platoon advantages to secure his spot as our premier 1B.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley**, whose 43.33 score nearly pushed him into the UTIL slot. Ultimately, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (50.31) edged him out, despite the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed arm, due to a superior raw base projection and a higher concentration of expected production. Elsewhere, **Jose Caballero** (60.15) remains a critical start for us; despite batting 8th, his aggressive platoon edge against a lefty and a helpful wind direction makes him a sneaky asset for SB volume. We are keeping a close watch on **Seiya Suzuki**, who landed on the bench at 41.70; his score was suppressed by a poor SP matchup and unfavorable wind, rendering him a secondary option compared to the volatility of our starting outfield. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Dalton Rushing** (49.29), as his utility is hampered by an elite opposing arm, though his projected involvement in potential base-stealing opportunities keeps him in the lineup over bench options like **Travis Bazzana** (40.14). While **Cole Young** (52.22) and **James Wood** (60.03) are clear starts, their reliance on favorable lineup positioning means any late scratch to the top of the order could dampen their efficiency. **Mickey Moniak** remains on our IL, leaving us to rely on our active depth to maintain our efficiency targets. As always, we are wary of any late-breaking weather shifts, but the current data suggests our core is well-positioned to maintain our competitive edge in stolen bases and counting stats.",
